From 2514bb12ce870c76188b851ff30ff9709ad50c75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HelaFaye <dilsha21@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:36:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] Board devices: OLEDs, touch, T-Deck keyboard, MCP23017,
 buttons

ssd1306/sh1106: I2C OLEDs (128x64, 128x32) as screens: control
bytes (Co, D/C#), addressing modes, windows, segment/COM remap, start
line, offset, contrast, invert, display on/off.

gt911, cst816, ft6336: capacitive touch controllers with their ID
and point registers, GT911 configuration and status handshake,
reports every 10 ms while touched with INT pulses (FT6336 polling: INT
low while touched); touches from the pointer or qom-set x/y/pressed.

tdeck-keyboard: LilyGO T-Deck's I2C keyboard (0x55): keys from the
host keyboard or qom-set keys, backlight commands.

mcp23017: 16 GPIO lines in and out, pull-ups, polarity, interrupt on
change or compare, INTA/INTB with MIRROR/ODR/INTPOL, INTCAP.

gpio-button: a button (or a rotary encoder's quadrature) on an S3 pin
or any device's GPIO input, pressed with qom-set or a host key.
